  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Just Landscape Transition plan for the Upper Groot Letaba catchment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment focuses on the development of a &#x2018;Just Landscape Transition plan&#x2019; for the upper Groot Letaba catchment (sub-catchments B81A and B81B and perhaps B81C/D/E as well), through a locally-led process. The Just Transition is a concept well-known in South Africa, and refers to a transition that should be greening the economy in a way that is fair and inclusive, creating decent work opportunities and leaving no one behind. In this case, the focus will be on a just transition within a sub-catchment, towards  sustainable water and land use, protection and restoration of endemic biodiversity and nature, while at the same time allowing for economic development of local communities, such as black emerging farmers. The Just Landscape Transition plan will include all these areas.The Just Landscape Transition plan has the goal of sustainably protecting water for nature, food and consumption. The plan will include a clear programme of activities and interventions to improve sustainable land and water use in the chosen sub catchment, resulting from a process of open dialogue between the main stakeholders. For this purpose, a multi-stakeholder platform will be organised and facilitated, to discuss and adopt goals, activities and the contents of the Plan. This landscape plan will be the main guidance for further development in the area, address water quality and quantity challenges, include a package of measures and long-term financial solutions to implement these measures at scale.</narrative>
  </description>
